── UNSATISFIED BOUND ────────────────── E0318_unsatisfied_bound.lt:1:57  [E0318]

`f64` doesn't implement `Hash`:

  1 │ fn by_price(prices: Map<f64, str>, price: f64) -> str { prices[price] }
    │                                                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

Using a trait's operation on a type parameter needs the bound, as `<T: Show>` to
interpolate a `T`. A type passed in implements the trait: write its `impl`, or
choose a type that has one.
